{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"5c254f15055b18d8ffa8f973a5f57158d3021f9d2dbf9068542855908ba00dde","slug":"introducing-the-technical-notes","location":"/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Introducing the Technical Notes","description":"The writing on this site that people want to cite now has its own series. A technical note is written like a short paper, gets an archival PDF, and carries a DOI that resolves to it.","keywords":["Underworld Code"],"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Louis Moresi","given":"Louis","family":"Moresi"},"name":"Louis Moresi","orcid":"0000-0003-3685-174X","affiliations":["Australian National University"],"id":"contributors-introducing-the-technical-notes-generated-uid-0"}],"affiliations":[{"id":"Australian National University","name":"Australian National University"}],"date":"2026-08-14","license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","free":true,"CC":true}},"open_access":true,"github":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org","source_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/blob/main/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/underworld-technical-notes/underworldcode.org/edit/main/articles/introducing-the-technical-notes/introducing-the-technical-notes.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"introducing-the-technical-notes.md","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/18c8c99505/build/introducing-the-tech-34423455eb668db512256b7e5f143e3f.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This site has always carried two kinds of writing. Some of it is news — a\nrelease, a workshop, a paper accepted. The rest is the sort of thing a reader\nlater wants to point at: how a solver actually behaves, what a benchmark\nmeasured, why a method works the way it does and where it stops working. The\ntwo have been mixed together, and there has been no way to cite the second\nkind.","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"tLlNcZyc6n"}],"key":"P5ZwIHcpVv"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So it now has its own series. A ","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"beb4hcgMtO"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"technical note","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"hEXjIz1aMG"}],"key":"Q4wW0C3tkP"},{"type":"text","value":" is written like a short\npaper. It carries a version, an archival PDF built from the same source as the\npage, and a DOI that resolves to that PDF. Deposit is deliberate rather than\nautomatic: a note is published here first, and only gets an identifier when we\ndecide it is worth one.","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"p7tTAkQRTp"}],"key":"REhP3MtxbI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The point is not formality. It is that we can write down what we measured, at\nthe length it takes to be useful, and then refer to it — from a paper, from an\nissue, from the next note — instead of describing it again.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"tUzz0velZw"}],"key":"CgHK0ss4UB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first two are up: ","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":